.antlr/
__pycache__
jets/bin/
jets/pkg/
jetstore.egg-info

# Workspace IDE build artifacts. node_modules is hundreds of megabytes and holds
# platform-native binaries (esbuild, rollup) built for the developer's machine,
# so shipping it into the build context would be both slow and wrong; the image
# installs its own from package-lock.json. dist is rebuilt in the image too.
jetsclient_ide/node_modules/
jetsclient_ide/dist/

# Python virtual environments and tool caches under tools/. **The same argument
# as node_modules above, and it was measured rather than predicted** (P9-I61):
# `Dockerfile.cpipes_python_lambda` copies `tools/cpipes_node` whole, and on a
# checkout where anybody has run `uv run` that directory holds a `.venv` of the
# developer's own wheels — 173 MB once pyarrow is a dependency, with
# platform-native extension modules in it. Measured: the image built to
# **916.8 MB** against **572.1 MB** from a clean checkout, the whole of the
# difference being that venv and the caches beside it. The image installs its own
# distributions from the source tree, so nothing here is needed at build time and
# what it would ship is one machine's binaries.
**/.venv/
**/venv/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/*.egg-info/
